submachine gun does to "immortal"?

240
00:21:19.258 --> 00:21:23.425
- Well. this ain't Chicago.
You can't just shoot him.

241
00:21:23.425 --> 00:21:27.133
Do that. people from around here
will string us up from a tree.

242
00:21:29.883 --> 00:21:32.300
- Do I look stupid to you?

243
00:21:32.467 --> 00:21:35.300
I've been brought in to do a job.

244
00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:38.758
And I know just who to start with.

245
00:21:41.758 --> 00:21:43.592
- You know something?

246
00:21:44.300 --> 00:21:46.800
I don't much like you.

247
00:21:47.883 --> 00:21:50.508
- Yeah? Well. not many do.

248
00:22:06.258 --> 00:22:08.592
Gimme some of that.

249
00:22:08.592 --> 00:22:10.508
Yeah. it's good.

250
00:22:15.967 --> 00:22:19.592
- I could run them blockades.

251
00:22:19.717 --> 00:22:22.175
- You? A blockader?

252
00:22:22.175 --> 00:22:23.758
Shit!
- What do you mean. shit?

253
00:22:23.758 --> 00:22:27.425
Danny. I can drive
a damn sight better than you can.

254
00:22:27.425 --> 00:22:29.300
Just not in the shitcan we got.

255
00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:32.050
- Oh. yeah? Well. Forrest.
he don't wanna hear about it.

256
00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:33.842
Yeah. well...

257
00:22:34.342 --> 00:22:36.258
The hell with Forrest.

258
00:22:36.258 --> 00:22:39.258
I'm sick of being his house dog.

259
00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:46.550
- You wanna tell him that?
Or you want me to do that. too?

260
00:22:51.467 --> 00:22:54.133
You alright there. Jack?
- Shut up. Howard.

261
00:22:54.133 --> 00:22:56.675
Forrest ain't got no aspirations.

262
00:22:56.675 --> 00:23:00.842
He still sleeps on a mattress
on the floor like a fucking Chinaman.

263
00:23:01.092 --> 00:23:04.467
- You might wanna watch your mouth
there. little brother.

264
00:23:04.550 --> 00:23:07.342
- Fuck off. Howard.

265
00:23:07.925 --> 00:23:09.925
- Oh. come on.
- Stop. Stop.

266
00:23:09.925 --> 00:23:12.258
- It's...

267
00:23:14.633 --> 00:23:17.217
Where are you going with that stuff?

268
00:23:17.217 --> 00:23:18.550
- Church.

269
00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:21.967
Hell. you better
take it easy on that jar. then!

270
00:24:26.258 --> 00:24:28.425
- Let us pray.

271
00:24:29.008 --> 00:24:32.258
If any man loved the world...

272
00:24:32.550 --> 00:24:35.883
the love of the Father
is not in him.

273
00:24:36.425 --> 00:24:38.092
For all that is in the world.

274
00:24:38.092 --> 00:24:40.717
the lust of the flesh.

275
00:24:40.717 --> 00:24:43.592
and the lust of the eyes.

276
00:24:43.758 --> 00:24:45.925
and the pride of life.

277
00:24:45.925 --> 00:24:49.383
is not of the Father.
but is of the world.

278
00:24:51.592 --> 00:24:53.758
Amen.

279
00:24:53.758 --> 00:24:56.550
39. top.

280
00:26:35.175 --> 00:26:38.300
- Too much rust in the tank. maybe.

281
00:26:47.383 --> 00:26:49.550
Or lead.

282
00:26:57.717 --> 00:26:59.592
- Μind if I come in?

283
00:27:01.133 --> 00:27:04.675
- Don't expect no biscuits
coming out around here.

284
00:27:06.008 --> 00:27:07.092
- Who's that?

285
00:27:07.092 --> 00:27:09.133
- Aunt Winnie.

286
00:27:09.133 --> 00:27:12.383
- Why don't you tell Aunt Winnie
this is not a social visit?

287
00:27:12.383 --> 00:27:15.425
- Well. I ain't sure
that'll do no good. sir.

288
00:27:15.425 --> 00:27:18.133
She ain't right in the head.

289
00:27:23.508 --> 00:27:25.633
- Three things you've got to tell us. son.

290
00:27:25.633 --> 00:27:30.008
Where's the still? Where's the liquor?
And where's the money?

291
00:27:34.967 --> 00:27:36.800
He don't have it.

292
00:27:39.967 --> 00:27:41.800
- Now who might you be?

293
00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:45.467
That there is Jack Bondurant.

294
00:27:46.092 --> 00:27:48.383
Well. I'll be damned.

295
00:27:49.133 --> 00:27:51.717
I was told I'd find you here.

296
00:27:52.300 --> 00:27:54.467
And look.

297
00:27:57.133 --> 00:27:59.300
Here you are.

298
00:28:00.508 --> 00:28:03.342
Go find the still. Leave us alone.

299
00:28:11.008 --> 00:28:14.633
So. the runt of the litter.

300
00:28:14.967 --> 00:28:17.467
You boys don't get it. do you?

301
00:28:20.008 --> 00:28:22.217
Look at me. son.

302
00:28:27.675 --> 00:28:30.383
Oh. you're a peach.

303
00:28:34.300 --> 00:28:36.425
- What's going on?

304
00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:44.008
Come closer.

305
00:28:44.592 --> 00:28:47.008
Step forward.

306
00:28:50.258 --> 00:28:52.508
Stop right there.

307
00:29:09.175 --> 00:29:11.300
Get up.

308
00:29:16.050 --> 00:29:20.300
I thought they said you Bondurant boys
were hard-boiled sons of bitches.

309
00:29:29.217 --> 00:29:31.800
Oh. this is terrible.

310
00:29:33.008 --> 00:29:35.050
This just won't do.

311
00:29:48.258 --> 00:29:50.383
- Μy brothers are gonna get you.

312
00:29:50.383 --> 00:29:52.133
They're gonna kill you.

313
00:29:52.133 --> 00:29:53.925
- Is that so?

314
00:29:53.925 --> 00:29:56.800
That's not gonna help you
right now. is it?

315
00:30:02.758 --> 00:30:05.342
Why don't you tell
those brothers of yours

316
00:30:05.342 --> 00:30:07.967
we're coming for them next?

317
00:30:12.050 --> 00:30:13.800
You tell 'em.

318
00:30:14.008 --> 00:30:15.717
No more!

319
00:30:16.175 --> 00:30:18.383
No more. please!

320
00:30:21.800 --> 00:30:23.800
Don't touch me!

321
00:30:33.175 --> 00:30:36.175
Next time. I'll come down real hard.

322
00:31:27.300 --> 00:31:29.425
- Alright.

323
00:31:32.258 --> 00:31:35.175
So you wanna get into this racket.

324
00:31:36.550 --> 00:31:41.300
But I see you sitting there
looking like somebody's punching bag.

325
00:31:43.717 --> 00:31:46.050
So I ask you...

326
00:31:47.133 --> 00:31:49.842
what do you intend to do now?

327
00:31:51.675 --> 00:31:54.592
- What do I intend to do?
- Yeah.

328
00:31:56.508 --> 00:31:58.383
You.

329
00:32:00.675 --> 00:32:02.592
You expect somebody else to handle it?

330
00:32:02.592 --> 00:32:03.967
- No.
- Howard. maybe?

331
00:32:03.967 --> 00:32:07.008
- That ain't what I meant.
- What did you mean?

332
00:32:07.133 --> 00:32:09.383
- I don't need no help.

333
00:32:09.550 --> 00:32:11.800
I'm sorry?

334
00:32:11.925 --> 00:32:14.967
- I don't need no help.
- You don't?

335
00:32:18.550 --> 00:32:20.550
Here it is.

336
00:32:21.508 --> 00:32:24.300
As long as you are my brother.

337
00:32:24.300 --> 00:32:26.883
you will never let this happen again.
understand?

338
00:32:26.883 --> 00:32:29.883
- I get it.
- I don't think you do.

339
00:32:32.717 --> 00:32:35.050
- What if I can't?

340
00:32:37.008 --> 00:32:41.717
You know I'm not built like you
and Howard. I ain't never been like you.

341
00:32:42.717 --> 00:32:44.883
- That's alright.

342
00:32:48.842 --> 00:32:50.842
Jack...

343
00:32:52.675 --> 00:32:56.425
It is not the violence
that sets a man apart.

344
00:32:57.008 --> 00:33:00.883
Alright? It is the distance
that he is prepared to go.

345
00:33:03.217 --> 00:33:05.383
Jack. look at me.

346
00:33:06.133 --> 00:33:08.217
We are survivors.

347
00:33:08.217 --> 00:33:11.050
We control the fear.

348
00:33:11.175 --> 00:33:16.550
And without the fear.
we are all as good as dead.

349
00:33:19.925 --> 00:33:21.883
Do you understand?

350
00:33:22.342 --> 00:33:23.508
Do you?

351
00:33:23.508 --> 00:33:27.092
- Rakes told me to tell you
they're coming for you next.

352
00:33:27.217 --> 00:33:29.592
- Hmm.

353
00:33:30.342 --> 00:33:33.592
Yeah. well. they'll be back.
You can be sure of that.

354
00:33:37.675 --> 00:33:39.633
Erm...

355
00:33:43.383 --> 00:33:46.258
A present from your preacher friend.

356
00:33:49.967 --> 00:33:52.092
You gonna open it?

357
00:34:04.633 --> 00:34:07.508
- Fuck you. Howard.

358
00:34:08.467 --> 00:34:10.175
- Damn.

359
00:34:10.258 --> 00:34:12.467
Oh. damn.

360
00:34:52.300 --> 00:34:53.925
- Forrest Bondurant.

361
00:34:53.925 --> 00:34:58.842
It seems you've been involved
in certain illegal activities.

362
00:34:59.258 --> 00:35:02.217
- Illegal activities. huh?

363
00:35:02.675 --> 00:35:05.175
Hmm.
- Look here. Forrest.

364
00:35:05.300 --> 00:35:10.342
If you play ball with us. we can make
this here summons disappear.

365
00:35:11.217 --> 00:35:14.342
- You trying to shake me down. Henry?

366
00:35:16.467 --> 00:35:19.300
- I'm just the messenger here. Forrest.

367
00:35:23.133 --> 00:35:25.300
- Have you met Howard?

368
00:35:26.967 --> 00:35:30.342
- Oh. you're gonna shoot me. huh?
- Howard!

369
00:35:30.717 --> 00:35:33.508
Huh? Huh?

370
00:35:35.842 --> 00:35:38.425
You gonna hurt my brother?

371
00:35:38.717 --> 00:35:41.050
Huh. you trying to intimidate us.
Sheriff?

372
00:35:41.050 --> 00:35:43.050
Huh?

373
00:35:44.217 --> 00:35:46.467
The Bondurants?

374
00:35:48.883 --> 00:35:50.675
- Alright now. That's enough now.

375
00:35:50.675 --> 00:35:54.550
Think we're gonna sell out
like them other cocksuckers?

376
00:35:55.300 --> 00:35:58.883
- Huh? Huh?
- That's enough now.

377
00:36:01.258 --> 00:36:03.342
Howard. that's enough.

378
00:36:03.342 --> 00:36:05.800
Alright.

379
00:36:08.133 --> 00:36:10.633
You old piece of shit.

380
00:36:10.633 --> 00:36:13.217
You oughta know better
than to come here

381
00:36:13.217 --> 00:36:16.758
when Howard's been on
the stump whiskey for a few days.

382
00:36:17.175 --> 00:36:19.717
I think you might wanna
get out of here.

383
00:36:20.550 --> 00:36:25.300
You give my regards
to Special Deputy Rakes.

384
00:36:25.300 --> 00:36:27.592
Oh. yeah.

385
00:36:34.842 --> 00:36:37.842
It ain't nothing personal. Henry.

386
00:36:44.967 --> 00:36:47.300
He's got that special look
in his eye.

387
00:36:47.300 --> 00:36:49.300
- I don't.
- He does.

388
00:36:49.300 --> 00:36:52.258
Yes. you do.

389
00:37:10.175 --> 00:37:12.467
- I saw you at the Bondurant place.

390
00:37:17.258 --> 00:37:19.550
You're not from around here.

391
00:37:20.925 --> 00:37:22.842
Chicago. right?

392
00:37:27.425 --> 00:37:32.092
You were a dancer up there.
The Apex Club. wasn't it?

393
00:37:32.092 --> 00:37:35.883
Did a little number with feathers.
I believe.

394
00:37:39.508 --> 00:37:41.967
Something troubling you?

395
00:37:42.092 --> 00:37:45.883
- Get out of my way.
- You don't need to worry about me.

396
00:37:46.133 --> 00:37:49.675
I ain't the kind
to drink from a greasy cup.

397
00:37:54.467 --> 00:37:56.925
Where's Jack?

398
00:37:57.050 --> 00:38:00.467
- I've seen him swanning around
in Daddy's old suit.

399
00:38:00.842 --> 00:38:03.092
- Listen. Howard.
- Yeah?

400
00:38:03.092 --> 00:38:05.800
- I need you here with me tonight.

401
00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:09.008
I got business with out-of-towners
I never dealt with before.

402
00:38:09.008 --> 00:38:12.383
- Yeah? Where they from?
- Chicago.

403
00:38:14.050 --> 00:38:17.217
- Yeah. well. me and Danny.
we just gotta stop by the stills first.

404
00:38:17.217 --> 00:38:20.133
- You just be here by eleven now.
You got that?

405
00:38:20.133 --> 00:38:24.508
I got it.
When have I ever let you down?

406
00:38:32.508 --> 00:38:35.342
<i>Come walk with me through the pines</i>

407
00:38:35.342 --> 00:38:38.425
<i>In the morning sun</i>

408
00:38:42.508 --> 00:38:48.092
<i>Birds singing in the pines
in the morning sun</i>

409
00:38:51.300 --> 00:38:53.967
- How'd you like to go for a ride
with me sometime?

410
00:38:53.967 --> 00:38:58.217
- You must be jingle-brained if you think I'm
gonna get in a car with the likes of you.

411
00:38:58.675 --> 00:39:01.883
Anyway. you oughta be worried
if my father catches you here.

412
00:39:01.883 --> 00:39:03.425
Talking to me.

413
00:39:03.425 --> 00:39:06.383
He's just in the feed store there.

414
00:39:07.092 --> 00:39:09.467
- Why'd I need to be worried?

415
00:39:09.842 --> 00:39:12.467
- You know. coming to
the church meeting like that.

416
00:39:12.467 --> 00:39:15.633
Then busting out of there
like a crazy person.

417
00:39:15.633 --> 00:39:18.092
Are you affected in the head?

418
00:39:18.758 --> 00:39:21.425
- Hold on now. look here. Look.

419
00:39:21.425 --> 00:39:24.633
Would a crazy person
wear a suit as fancy as this?

420
00:39:25.008 --> 00:39:27.717
- It still don't explain
why you acted like a lunatic.

421
00:39:27.717 --> 00:39:30.550
- I didn't want my feet washed. is all.

422
00:39:31.967 --> 00:39:35.050
- I know who you are.
- Oh. yeah? Who's that?

423
00:39:35.050 --> 00:39:39.175
- One of them Bondurant boys.
and that's enough.

424
00:39:39.383 --> 00:39:42.508
There ain't many that have
a good word to say about you.

425
00:39:42.508 --> 00:39:45.592
- Yeah?
- Except some rubbish about a legend.

426
00:39:45.592 --> 00:39:47.425
- Yeah?

427
00:39:47.425 --> 00:39:50.883
- About you guys being invincible
or some such nonsense.

428
00:39:50.883 --> 00:39:53.675
- Say that word again. What'd you say?

429
00:39:53.717 --> 00:39:56.842
- Invincible.
- Shoot. I don't know what that means.

430
00:39:56.842 --> 00:39:59.008
Sounds good. though.

431
00:39:59.633 --> 00:40:03.758
- Μy daddy thinks you boys are
the worst thing ever to hit Franklin.

432
00:40:03.758 --> 00:40:06.342
- What would your daddy know?

433
00:40:07.133 --> 00:40:10.633
- You sure got a funny way
of courting. Jack Bondurant.

434
00:40:11.175 --> 00:40:14.258
That is what you're doing. right?
Courting?

435
00:40:15.842 --> 00:40:17.758
- Yeah.

436
00:40:20.675 --> 00:40:22.800
Alright. then.

437
00:40:23.967 --> 00:40:26.800
Well. you tell your daddy I said hi.

438
00:40:28.800 --> 00:40:30.300
Oh...!

439
00:40:30.300 --> 00:40:32.300
Thank you.

440
00:40:47.217 --> 00:40:49.800
Oh!

441
00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:57.592
- Oh. shit!

442
00:41:15.050 --> 00:41:18.633
- Hey. Red. Where them feathers at?

443
00:41:30.175 --> 00:41:32.133
- He's a cripple. Don't worry about it.

444
00:41:32.133 --> 00:41:34.258
Hey. Forrest.

445
00:41:39.425 --> 00:41:42.550
- Alright. go tell Μaggie
to shut her down.

446
00:41:46.925 --> 00:41:50.592
Alright now! That's enough.
Come on now. get out of here.

447
00:41:53.383 --> 00:41:57.592
- I paid for another jar
and she won't give it.

448
00:41:57.592 --> 00:42:00.008
And then the bitch done me!

449
00:42:00.300 --> 00:42:01.592
- No. you didn't.

450
00:42:01.592 --> 00:42:04.175
- We gonna buy near 100 gallons
of your liquor.

451
00:42:04.175 --> 00:42:06.717
Now you ain't gonna throw in some extra?

452
00:42:06.717 --> 00:42:08.758
- You ain't buying a thing.
Get out of here.

453
00:42:08.758 --> 00:42:13.175
He pulled a gun on her.
then she pulled the knife and cut him.

454
00:42:15.550 --> 00:42:18.008
- Did you pull a gun on this woman?

455
00:42:20.217 --> 00:42:22.342
Forrest!

456
00:42:28.717 --> 00:42:30.758
- I may be a cripple boy.
you sack of shit.

457
00:42:30.758 --> 00:42:33.800
but I'll blow your goddamn brains out
if you move!

458
00:42:42.842 --> 00:42:46.217
- Alright now. Sorry.

459
00:43:41.592 --> 00:43:44.092
Well. you best be getting home.

460
00:43:44.925 --> 00:43:47.092
- OK.

461
00:43:59.133 --> 00:44:02.050
Are you sure you're alright?

462
00:44:09.258 --> 00:44:12.592
- A bit too much whoopee for one night.
I guess.

463
00:44:22.217 --> 00:44:24.800
Bye. Forrest.

464
00:45:18.675 --> 00:45:21.175
- Well. that don't make no sense.

465
00:45:33.550 --> 00:45:36.758
- Now you got trouble.

466
00:45:50.092 --> 00:45:52.675
- Fucking hillbilly!

467
00:46:20.675 --> 00:46:25.675
("Aim Toward the Sky" by The Bootleggers
feat Liela Μoss and Emmylou Harris)

468
00:46:42.092 --> 00:46:44.300
- Damn.

469
00:46:50.800 --> 00:46:55.133
<i>So you'll aim</i>

470
00:46:55.133 --> 00:46:58.675
<i>Towards the sky</i>

471
00:46:58.842 --> 00:47:02.633
<i>And you'll rise</i>

472
00:47:06.425 --> 00:47:10.425
<i>High today</i>

473
00:47:14.217 --> 00:47:18.133
<i>Fly away</i>

474
00:47:21.425 --> 00:47:25.842
<i>Forrest?
Far away</i>

475
00:47:29.800 --> 00:47:34.217
<i>Far from pain</i>

476
00:47:36.050 --> 00:47:38.050
Forrest?

477
00:47:45.925 --> 00:47:48.592
There's something you need to know.

478
00:47:54.925 --> 00:47:58.800
Now we're gonna have some fun.

479
00:48:39.758 --> 00:48:43.258
You can come in.
but don't let him talk.

480
00:48:53.800 --> 00:48:55.842
- Hey. Forrest.

481
00:48:57.508 --> 00:49:00.383
Them doctors are saying
you walked in here.

482
00:49:01.883 --> 00:49:04.592
All the ways from Blackwater Station!

483
00:49:04.883 --> 00:49:08.050
Through the damn snow!

484
00:49:13.217 --> 00:49:15.467
Did you get them. Forrest?

485
00:49:17.842 --> 00:49:22.633
Cos I wanna be there when you do.
I'll hold them down myself.

486
00:49:23.133 --> 00:49:26.050
Shoot! Walking all the way here
from Blackwater Station!

487
00:49:26.050 --> 00:49:29.300
- Jack. why don't you shut up a minute.
huh?

488
00:49:50.467 --> 00:49:53.383
- You should've been there. Howard.

489
00:50:31.675 --> 00:50:34.592
- Look what they did to you.

490
00:50:43.675 --> 00:50:46.675
I'm leaving. Forrest.

491
00:50:48.092 --> 00:50:49.883
- Huh.

492
00:50:51.175 --> 00:50:54.842
Well. it ain't really the quiet life
you were looking for. huh?

493
00:50:54.842 --> 00:50:57.800
- Those people. Forrest.

494
00:51:00.342 --> 00:51:02.717
People like them?

495
00:51:02.717 --> 00:51:05.342
They're why I left Chicago.

496
00:51:07.133 --> 00:51:09.758
